# The leak check, and only the leak check.
#
# `husky init` writes `npm test` here by default. That is wrong for this repo:
# the suite boots a real server against a throwaway data directory and drives
# it over HTTP, so a full run is tens of seconds — and a hook that slow gets
# bypassed with --no-verify the first time someone is in a hurry. A hook people
# routinely skip is worse than no hook. Correctness is CI's job, and CI already
# runs the whole suite on two Node versions.
#
# This one is here because CI *cannot* do its job later. CI runs after the
# commit has reached a public repository, at which point a leaked word is in
# the git history, publicly and permanently — reverting does not remove it,
# because GitHub keeps unreachable objects fetchable and any fork keeps its own
# copy. A CI failure there is a fire alarm that rings after the building has
# burned.
#
# It is also the only layer where the vocabulary half runs at all. The word
# list is gitignored and never published, so it exists where someone is
# writing, not on a runner. See scripts/check-leak.mjs.
npm run check:leak
